{"kind":"request","text":"Scenario harness typed from a declared definition, with strict assertions.\n\nExtend dap's scenario harness so an author can write a scenario against a declared definition with editor-time types and strict assertions, and run it in memory in under a second.\n\nSource: Hugh's request of 28 October 2026, after a review of the alchemy Domain package, whose Story harness has these properties. The planner may attach this to an existing work item or sequence it; the request stands on its own.\n\nToday: `dap check` runs JSON scenarios (steps act, expect, save, projection; examples/grow/check/fault-scenario.json) through Core and SQLite. The typed handle `declaredHandle` checks an intent's fields against the definition before signing. The judges of `derive` run in memory. A scenario's expectation is the answer; nothing fails a scenario because an entry, effect, send or timed firing happened that the scenario did not assert.\n\nWanted:\n1. A TypeScript form of a scenario whose steps are typed from the definition: act kinds, their fields, item types and slots, refusal names. A wrong field or an unknown act is an editor error, not a runtime finding.\n2. Steps for: given (entries already applied), when (one signed act, one delivery, or a clock advance), then (the entries, effects, sends and attention the act produced), refused (reason and name), state (an item's slots and state afterwards), and a clock step for timed rules.\n3. Strictness: a scenario fails when the act produced an entry, effect, send or timed firing that no step asserted, and when a step asserts something that did not happen.\n4. Runs on the derive judges in memory with no storage. The same scenario also runs through Core and SQLite (the `dap check` route) with one switch, as the lanes scenarios do today.\n5. The JSON scenario format stays; the typed form is a way to write it, and `dap check` accepts both.\n6. Documentation in docs/write-an-application.md under \"Write scenarios\", and one scenario of the lending library converted as the example.","body":{"conditions":"Landed on main with the typed scenario harness, the strict assertion rule, one converted lending scenario and the docs; or superseded by a planner act naming the request that carries this work.","target_head":"0881c1bca1df31a9fdb4ae72947cbbedf1b3ec51","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}